answer.worked:
For the $y$-intercept, set $x=0$.
$$\begin{align*}
y &= 2\sin\left(-\frac{\pi}{3}\right) \\
&= -\sqrt{3}
\end{align*}$$
For the $x$-intercepts, set $y=0$.
$$\begin{align*}
2\sin\left(2x-\frac{\pi}{3}\right) &= 0 \\
2x-\frac{\pi}{3} &= n\pi \\
x &= \frac{\pi}{6}+\frac{n\pi}{2}
\end{align*}$$
For $0\leq x\leq \pi$, $x=\frac{\pi}{6}$ and $x=\frac{2\pi}{3}$.
The intercepts are $(0,-\sqrt{3})$, $\left(\frac{\pi}{6},0\right)$ and $\left(\frac{2\pi}{3},0\right)$.

